// The icon set, as path data.
//
// Three approaches were possible and only one of them works here. The `icons` crate
// targets Leptos and Dioxus, expanding to web component macros a Slint interface
// cannot use. Slint 1.17 ships no SVG decoder, so `@image-url` on an `.svg` is out.
// What Slint does have is `Path`, which takes SVG path syntax and renders it
// natively — no decoding, no asset files, resolution-independent, and tinted per
// theme. That is better than either alternative, not a fallback from them.
//
// One family throughout: a 24-unit grid, a 1.6-unit stroke, round caps and joins.
// That consistency is what makes a toolbar look designed rather than collected, and
// it is the first thing lost when icons are picked one at a time from different sets.
//
// Generated. Edit the generator, not this file.

import { Tokens } from "@iris/theme/tokens.slint";

